(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRuleApply", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"60042bd1-2e2a-c849-aa3f-cd9805d0a483"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRuleApply", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "hg"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"97141ebb-4a00-7e4b-bece-3d6ff0b76d96"],
 " ",
 "applies rule to the hypergraph hg, giving a list of events, one for every \
way the rule's input matches."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"9fbba7a0-c7de-1e4c-8fae-7c0b4ec85011"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"98d1a8c4-c6f1-c242-b8be-05dd9c530491"],
 " ",
 "is equivalent."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"22be8d79-95c5-7e48-b34a-fa5b29971f71"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"dedac4f4-0b86-444b-aaab-9d00ee5017fc"],

Cell["\<\
Each event is an association. \"Hypergraph\" is the result; \
\"MatchVertices\", \"MatchEdges\" and \"MatchEdgePositions\" say what was \
matched; \"NewVertices\" and \"NewEdges\" what was created; \"DeletedVertices\
\" what was destroyed; \"RuleVertexMap\" the correspondence from the rule's \
vertices to the hypergraph's; and \"Rule\" the rule itself.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"94164524-b3d1-964c-8c09-1d4610920aac"],

Cell["\<\
The result is the hypergraph with the matched edges removed and the output's \
edges put in their place. A vertex the output introduces becomes a new vertex \
of the result, and one the output drops is destroyed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c612bd89-8a2b-a241-a301-f9b6a7a75670"],

Cell["\<\
A destroyed vertex is removed only when nothing still standing uses it. A \
rule rewrites what it matched, and reaching into edges it did not match to \
strike a vertex out of them would not be local; so a vertex the rule drops \
but another edge still holds simply stays, and is not reported destroyed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bba6047c-5622-2d4b-b220-3d6b52543fb0"],

Cell["\<\
New vertices are named so as to miss every vertex already present, which \
makes the result reproducible from one session to the next rather than \
depending on a counter of fresh symbols.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"469b4f0c-d801-cd4b-b5be-45cf012bdbf4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Labels constrain matching and absence of a label does not: a pattern edge \
or vertex carrying no label matches whatever it lies on, and one carrying a \
label matches only the same label. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c0eace05-9c46-c046-a169-216db5eb0963"],
 " ignores labels altogether."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0fd8d7da-c2db-e64e-9db5-ee7735bc195c"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types must agree, and the pattern is matched over the orderings its \
symmetry allows: one for a directed edge, its rotations for a cyclic one, \
every permutation for an unordered one. An unordered edge of arity k \
therefore matches in k! ways, which are genuinely different matches and are \
all reported.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6bfc31bb-c062-3645-8acc-2a85ef8873fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<DistinctVertices\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], 
   "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "41e41e23-76fa-d84b-85bd-c6be6a19a770"],
 ", the default, keeps two vertices of the input from landing on one vertex \
of the hypergraph, which is what the reference paclet does. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["False", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7c4d487a-5ac8-294c-a15f-ef0c732c3dbc"],
 " allows it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b7506810-dc3b-4c46-b949-d2f1f166d86f"],

Cell["\<\
No match gives an empty list, which is not a failure: it says the rule does \
not apply.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"167be4a6-3319-0248-933f-814e57c2151b"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"69f6fa53-7ca2-154b-b92b-ee3c3db73be5"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge of a two-edge path: one event for each edge.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"0c7ed093-875c-c846-b70b-52f4a2b83896"],

Cell["\<\
sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}];
chain = Hypergraph[{Edge[{1, 2}], Edge[{2, 3}]}];
events = sub[chain];
Length[events]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f86678ea-34ed-384f-92b7-e102ad69124d"],

Cell[BoxData["2"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"279d4520-6bf6-bc4a-b8db-4152145a6f8f"],

Cell["What the first event did:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"343c9442-eea1-0a4e-9b0b-32570cf336e6"],

Cell["\<\
KeyTake[First[events], {\"MatchEdgePositions\", \"NewVertices\", \
\"RuleVertexMap\"}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"59389d8b-cd9f-d14e-a257-3d0c7f45ef2c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"MatchEdgePositions\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"NewVertices\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[FormalV]", "[", "1", "]"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"RuleVertexMap\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"\[FormalV]", "[", "1", "]"}]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}]}],
   "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"c1487ba1-b7bd-ae4a-\
b36d-58f8be9d1821"],

Cell["And what it produced:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"da6171ff-9e66-6f4f-b3c0-5d79d0a6efcb"],

Cell["First[events][\"Hypergraph\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"545a5087-d393-fb49-9a30-faad6bc126d7"],

